RAYSHADE 4.0 on OS-9/68K -- it runs, and the pictures are wrong===============================================================A full ray tracer: eleven primitives (blob, box, cone, cylinder, heightfield, plane, polygon, sphere, torus, triangles), CSG, five light sourcetypes, solid procedural texturing, bump and image mapping, jitteredantialiasing.  Craig Kolb et al.  Copyright in DOC/rayshade/Copyright.WHAT WORKS    rayshade -R 64 48 -O out.pic /dd/GAMES/rayshade/boxball.ray  It runs, preprocesses the scene, traces, reports full statistics, and  writes an image file of exactly the right size.  Verified.  It needs `cccp', and it needs a `shell'.  Rayshade runs every scene  file through the C preprocessor, and it does that with popen() --  which on OS-9 forks a program called `shell'.  THIS DISK HAS NO  `shell': it has bash and sh.  And the shell that gets forked looks a  command up in the DATA directory, so cccp has to be at /dd rather  than in CMDS.  Both, and it renders -- MEASURED 2026-08-28:      copy /dd/CMDS/sh /dd/CMDS/shell      copy /dd/CMDS/GCC139/gcc_cccp /dd/cccp      rayshade -R 32 24 -O /dd/tmp/out.pic /dd/GAMES/rayshade/boxball.ray  Without the first: `popen of "cccp ..." failed!'.  Without the  second: `cccp: nowhere found' and `Nothing to be rendered.'  Without it you get:  shell: can't execute "cccp"  followed by  "rayshade: Fatal error: Nothing to be rendered."  Output is rayshade's GENERIC format, not Utah RLE -- this build was made  without the Utah Raster Toolkit.  The file is plain ASCII "<w> <h>" then a  CR then w*h*3 bytes of interleaved RGB.  Easy to convert; rsconvert is  here too.WHAT IS WRONG  The images come out heavily blown out, and the adaptive-sampling numbers  in the statistics are nonsense -- "-262438.98 split", "842088.45 split".  Those are floating-point values that cannot be right.  This is NOT the general floating point being broken.  Measured separately:  os9exec computes sqrt, exp, sin, pow and long summations correctly when  linked against math881.l (see DOC/README-FLOATINGPOINT).  The likely cause is the build: the tree's own makefile compiles with      CCFLAGS = -mc68040 -mlong-calls -ob  under gcc, while os9exec emulates a 68020 with a 68881.  A 68040 targets a  different FPU with a smaller hardware instruction set.  That is a  hypothesis, not a finding -- it has not been confirmed.  So: the binary here may well be correct on the 68040 it was built for.  Do not assume the renderer is broken; assume the pairing is wrong.WHERE TO TAKE IT  Full source is in /dd/SRC/rayshade -- libray (six sub-libraries), libshade,  rayshade, rayview, raypaint and etc/RSCONVERT, each with its own OS-9  makefile.  Rebuilding it needs gcc, bison, and r68/l68.  A rebuild without  -mc68040 is the obvious next experiment and would settle the question.  rayview needs SGI GL and will not build here.  Fifteen example scenes are in /dd/GAMES/rayshade.